WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.983
[MUSIC]

00:00:02.983 --> 00:00:06.290
So this is the 2014 World Series ring.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:10.830
Every single full-time member of our staff
got a World Series ring, how cool is that?

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.495
&gt;&gt; Giants win!

00:00:12.495 --> 00:00:17.870
&gt;&gt; I think we know we're
part of something special.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:22.755
&gt;&gt; A World Series win for
the San Francisco Giants for

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:26.508
the third time in the last five years.

00:00:26.508 --> 00:00:29.194
&gt;&gt; Every April,
when the crowds start coming back in,

00:00:29.194 --> 00:00:32.931
when it's the start of the season,
there's this renewed sense of wow.

00:00:32.931 --> 00:00:35.128
[MUSIC]

00:00:35.128 --> 00:00:38.890
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; Something I love about working for

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:42.650
the Giants is that we have people
from all different backgrounds and

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.270
fields within the team.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:50.150
I'm not sure that anyone would've said
that there's a job description around

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:54.290
someone who's interested in sports and
real estate, but

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:55.590
that's what I wanted to do.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:59.397
And I figured out a way to pull
it together to get there, and

00:00:59.397 --> 00:01:02.139
I think everyone really has that in them.

00:01:02.139 --> 00:01:07.098
[MUSIC]

00:01:07.098 --> 00:01:12.192
The most interesting thing to me is
really seeing all of it come together,

00:01:12.192 --> 00:01:16.300
and seeing how things like finance,
and engineering, and

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:21.170
law have this really incredible
intersection In urban development.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:26.810
So the northernmost part of the project
site that is right across from the ball

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:32.590
park is going to be a new five-acre
regional park with waterfront access,

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:37.210
and recreation opportunities,
and retail along the park's edge.

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:42.269
And then there'll be 12 new buildings
with offices, and homes, and restaurants.

00:01:43.415 --> 00:01:48.600
60% of the seats in the ballpark have
a view of what's happening on Lot A today.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:53.688
So imagine in the future when that view,
instead of cars and parking lot,

00:01:53.688 --> 00:01:58.220
is of parks, and trees, and
beautiful new homes and buildings.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.979
[MUSIC]

00:02:01.979 --> 00:02:06.089
I think what excites me the most
around this sort of work is that

00:02:06.089 --> 00:02:10.689
it's going to be part of the city for
hopefully generations to come.

00:02:10.689 --> 00:02:16.731
[MUSIC]

00:02:16.731 --> 00:02:20.533
One of the things I remember learning
at the GSB was that we actually can

00:02:20.533 --> 00:02:22.880
experiment from time to time.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:25.650
And I have to remind myself of that.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:29.170
So sometimes when I'm stuck in
a situation, or I don't know

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:34.080
quite how to respond, I'll actively think
to myself, I'm just going to experiment.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.050
I'm going to try something I
don't think I would normally do,

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.540
because maybe that'll get me past this.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.759
And sure enough, it usually works.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:49.570
&gt;&gt; Here comes Pence,
here's the throw, not in time.

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:54.090
&gt;&gt; The biggest thing that I would share
is that if you think there's a place for

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:58.160
you out in the world that doesn't exist
yet and you want to go create it,

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.190
you absolutely can.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:02.310
That doesn't have to be sports,
that doesn't have to be baseball.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:06.535
That doesn't have to be the niche
intersection of real estate and baseball,

00:03:06.535 --> 00:03:08.811
but whatever it is for you, go find that.

00:03:08.811 --> 00:03:12.167
And the more you love it,
the better you're going to be.

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:22.167
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

